# rpg/art/doll/maps/stamps/boots_child.stamps: the child's boot, ONE drawing in five tilts (docs/MOTION_P2.md 4.2, 5.5; STYLE_P2
# 10). The child's own chunky foot (kin/child/legs/std's side idle: the B rows F-2..F-1, 5 and 6 px over a 6 px Ink sole; the
# boot's top row above it is the shin), hand-placed at each tilt, never sheared, squashed or tool-rotated: C0 flat (the
# planted foot), C1 toe-up 1:2 (heel strike: the sole stepping 2 / 2 / 2 up to the toe; 15 px), C2 heel-up 1:2 (motion fix
# round 2, R2-06: the contact's trailing foot on its toe pad, the heel TWO rows up: the sole 2 / 2 / 2, 18 px), C3 toe-off
# (rolled onto the toe, the sole 1 / 2 / 2: the down frame's trailing foot; 17 px), C4 pointed (fix round 2: C2 rolled onto
# its toe tip, the sole 2 / 2 / 1: the walk pass's swing foot, toe down and lifted 2 in front of the planted shin; 18 px).
# The square heel, the outline all round, the straight Ink sole. `n` near, `f` far (a value darker). origin = the ground
# pivot on the sole row (the heel of C0 / C1, the toe's last Ink pixel of C2 / C3 / C4). L entries mirrored and re-lit,
# never the plain mirror. Used by kin/child/legs/std.pxm and tips.pxm (`# put` comments, expanded there pixel for pixel).
use person
# C0 flat (the planted foot), R view: origin = the heel
stamp C0n R origin 0 2
|fihhf.
|fihhgf
|KKKKKK
regions
|BBBBB.
|BBBBBB
|OOOOOO
stamp C0f R origin 0 2
|fhhgf.
|fhhggf
|KKKKKK
regions
|BBBBB.
|BBBBBB
|OOOOOO
# C1 toe-up 1:2 (heel strike), R view: origin = the heel
